-- title:
--   Hecke maximal ideal from a curve-congruent eigenform
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a natural number, $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$, $L$ a nonzero natural number, $S_0$ a set of natural numbers, $g$ a cusp form of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(L)$, and $\mathfrak{m}$ an ideal of the integral closure $\overline{\mathbb{Z}}$ of $\mathbb{Z}$ in $\mathbb{C}$. Assume: $g$ is a normalised eigenform in the sense of the project predicate, i.e. its $q$-expansion coefficients (of width $1$) satisfy $a_1(g)=1$, $a_{mn}(g)=a_m(g)a_n(g)$ for coprime $m,n$, the recursion $a_{q^{r+2}}(g)=a_q(g)a_{q^{r+1}}(g)-q\,a_{q^r}(g)$ for primes $q\nmid L$ and $a_{q^{r+2}}(g)=a_q(g)a_{q^{r+1}}(g)$ for primes $q\mid L$; $\mathfrak{m}$ is maximal and contains the image of $p$; and for every prime $\ell$ with $(\ell:\mathbb{Z})\nmid\Delta_W$ and $\ell\notin S_0$ there is $a\in\overline{\mathbb{Z}}$ whose image in $\mathbb{C}$ equals $a_\ell(g)$ and with $a-a_\ell(W)\in\mathfrak{m}$, where $a_\ell(W)=\ell+1-\#(W\bmod \ell)$. Then the algebra `heckeAlgebra L 2 S₀`, the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-$2$ cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(L)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid L$, $\ell\notin S_0$ and $U_q$ for primes $q\mid L$, $q\notin S_0$, has a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}_2$ containing $p$ such that $T_\ell-a_\ell(W)\in\mathfrak{m}_2$ for every prime $\ell\notin S_0$ with $\ell\nmid L$ and $(\ell:\mathbb{Z})\nmid\Delta_W$.
--
--   This is the translation of a congruence between the Hecke eigenvalues of a normalised eigenform and the Frobenius traces of an elliptic curve into the language of maximal ideals of the Hecke algebra, the form in which the level-lowering arguments are run. It is used in the construction of Mazur-type realisations of the mod $p$ representation attached to the curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_of_isNormalizedEigenform.lean

